# On-premises runtime file for the RabbitMQ broker (docs/rabbitmq-dispatch/spec.md
# §11.2/§11.4). Copy to /etc/ieum/rabbitmq.env, replace the blank values, then
# set owner root:root and mode 0600.
#
# This file is used twice:
#   - as `docker compose --env-file` for the `ieum-broker` project, so
#     RABBITMQ_IMAGE_DIGEST resolves the `${RABBITMQ_IMAGE_DIGEST}` reference
#     in deploy/onprem/rabbitmq/compose.yml;
#   - as the container's own `env_file:`, so RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_* configure the
#     broker's bootstrap admin account and vhost on first boot.
#
# RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER is the operator/administrator account only (management
# UI login, tagged `administrator` by the broker itself). app-main and app-ai
# use their own `ieum_main`/`ieum_ai` accounts, provisioned separately by
# provision-rabbitmq.sh — never put those credentials in this file.
#
# Never commit real credentials or copy this file into GitHub Actions.

RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_VHOST=/ieum
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER=ieum_broker_admin
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS=
RABBITMQ_IMAGE_DIGEST=
